1. Purpose

This file contains the final eleven secondary research questions in the Global Social Experiment research agenda.

These questions govern how canonical repository content becomes:

* a scholarly article;
* a book;
* a conference presentation;
* a Substack publication;
* educational material;
* a public website response;
* a case study;
* a consulting deliverable;
* or a commercial implementation offering.

The repository must remain the authoritative source layer for derivative outputs.

Derivative outputs may summarize, interpret, organize, teach, or expand upon repository content, but they must not silently create new canonical findings.

