Part XVIII — Research Outputs

RQ216 — Repository as Canonical Source

Research Question

How should the repository serve as the canonical source for all derivative outputs?

Short Title

Canonical Repository Authority

Purpose

This question defines how books, articles, presentations, websites, reports, educational materials, and consulting outputs remain linked to the version-controlled research repository.

Required Derivative Metadata

Every material derivative output should identify:

repository-name
repository-path
repository-version
release-tag
source-files
source-chunks
extraction-date
author-or-editor
modifications
publication-status

Canonical Rule

When a derivative output conflicts with the current canonical repository:

1. identify whether the derivative used an earlier release;
2. determine whether the repository change was editorial, substantive, legal, technical, or breaking;
3. update or annotate the derivative where appropriate;
4. preserve the historical source version;
5. and prevent outdated derivative content from silently overriding current canonical material.

