RQ219 — Case-Study Selection by Output

Research Question

How should case studies be selected for the book versus the academic paper?

Short Title

Case-Study Selection Rules

Purpose

This question distinguishes broad narrative and applied cases from the smaller number of cases needed to support a focused scholarly contribution.

Book Case-Study Criteria

A case may be included in the book when it:

* clarifies a major Web4 concept;
* illustrates an implementation domain;
* supports public understanding;
* is appropriately classified;
* and has sufficient permissions.

Academic Article Case-Study Criteria

A case may be included in the article when it:

* directly addresses an article research question;
* has strong provenance;
* supports methodological analysis;
* can be described concisely;
* and does not introduce unnecessary scope.

