RQ220 — Academic Publication Threshold

Research Question

Which findings are sufficiently supported for academic publication?

Short Title

Scholarly Evidence Threshold

Purpose

This question establishes a minimum standard for presenting a repository conclusion as a scholarly finding.

Candidate Publication Requirements

* clear research question;
* documented methodology;
* traceable evidence;
* transparent coding or analysis;
* preserved dissent;
* verified external factual claims;
* explicit limitations;
* and a defined scholarly contribution.

Candidate Finding Categories

publishable-finding
publishable-with-limitations
methodological-observation
preliminary-result
hypothesis-only
future-research
not-supported

Publication Exclusions

A claim should not be presented as an academic finding when it depends primarily on:

* unsupported model output;
* promotional language;
* repeated internal assertions;
* unverified legal claims;
* unverifiable institutional participation;
* or researcher preference without supporting evidence.

