RQ221 — Findings Versus Future Research

Research Question

Which findings should remain hypotheses or future research?

Short Title

Unresolved and Preliminary Claims

Purpose

This question prevents premature publication or implementation of claims that remain insufficiently supported.

Keep as a Hypothesis When

* supporting evidence is limited;
* the claim is interpretive;
* cross-model agreement is unstable;
* alternative explanations remain strong;
* legal verification is incomplete;
* implementation evidence is absent;
* or independent replication has not occurred.

Keep as Future Research When

* required data do not yet exist;
* institutional permission is pending;
* participant research is not approved;
* technology is immature;
* the question depends on future implementation;
* or the issue is too broad for the current study.

Required Labels

hypothesis
provisional-finding
unresolved
deferred
future-research

