Canonical Principle

The repository is the source of record.

The article, book, conference presentation, website, curriculum, and consulting materials are controlled derivatives.

The governing chain is:

canonical-source
→ versioned-claim
→ evidence-map
→ output-specific-selection
→ explicit-interpretation
→ limitations
→ publication
→ correction-and-version-tracking

A derivative output may make the research easier to understand, but it must not make the evidence appear stronger than it is.